From: bakhodirovxz <bohodirovasadbek1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:25:27 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/22] engine: keep shared trees through fill, sort, paste and
 structural edits

- Fill, Range Fill, sort and paste make copies with `Formula::copied`, which share the source's
  tree instead of building a new one per cell (filling a column down no longer costs a tree per
  cell). Cut and paste on the same sheet keeps the formula as it is.
- The workbook-wide rewrites (insert/delete rows, columns and cells, cut, sheet rename and delete,
  table rename) store the rewritten formulas through `FormulaRuns`, so a run whose references all
  moved the same way keeps sharing one tree. Delete Sheet and Rename Table no longer rewrite
  formulas they leave unchanged.

`tests/formula_templates.rs` runs each of these commands on a workbook as the reader gives it and
on the same workbook with every formula held on its own, and requires the same cells after every
command and after saving and reopening.
